{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "4ef0eea9-a117-84b2-b69c-0ba1375868e5",
  "created_at": "2026-01-13T11:30:36-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Nilza Brito",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T11:28:28-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T11:28:32-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, hello, Kevin. Hello. My name is Nilza Brito, I'm over on Farewell Street, three thirteen, in the North End. Hold on, I have something on the stove, let me turn this down. [pause] Okay. I'm sorry, my kitchen is so small, I turn around and I knock the pot."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T11:28:48-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem at all, Ms. Brito. Take your time. What's going on on Farewell Street?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T11:28:53-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, there's a big limb down on the sidewalk. A big one, from the tree out front. It came down after that coastal storm, the one that ended Saturday. I heard it crack Friday night, and I thought, that's the end of that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T11:29:07-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, big limb on the sidewalk, Farewell Street, came down in the storm. Is it blocking the whole sidewalk?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T11:29:14-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Most of it. People are walking out in the street around it, and with the cars, I worry. My mother used to say a tree falls the way it wants, she grew up with a pear tree, oh, it dropped pears all over, we made so much jam. [pause] I'm sorry, Kevin. I wander."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T11:29:31-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're fine. So, is the tree on city property, or does it belong to the house? Do you know?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T11:29:38-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's what I'm asking you. Who do I call? I rent, so it isn't mine, but is it the city, or the owner, or the electric company? There are wires up there, I don't know if the limb touched them."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T11:29:51-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good question. If it's in the street tree strip by the sidewalk, that's usually the city's, and we'd send someone to look. If it's touching wires, stay clear and the utility handles that part. I'm writing down three thirteen Farewell, limb across the sidewalk. I'll put in a request for our tree crew to check it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T11:30:08-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, that's wonderful. Should I call my landlord too?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T11:30:12-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wouldn't hurt to let him know. And if you see the limb on a wire or sparking, call the utility right away. Is this a good number for you, the one you're on?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T11:30:23-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, it's four oh one, five five five, zero one seven zero."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T11:30:27-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. Someone will follow up. Keep people off that spot if you can."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T11:30:32-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I will. Thank you, Kevin. God bless. Now my rice is burning."
    }
  ],
